    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `format_for_display` in `app/report.py`, and all 4 tests pass, including 2 new ones.\n\n**How it works:** it formats every cell with `table.map(...)`, which returns a new DataFrame and leaves the input unchanged. The index and columns stay the same. No dependencies were added.\n- `12500` \u2192 `\"12,500.00\"`\n- `-634.2` \u2192 `\"(634.20)\"`\n- `0` \u2192 `\"-\"`\n- missing \u2192 `\"\"`\n\n**One choice to check:** a value counts as zero if it rounds to zero at two decimals, so it shows as `\"-\"`. Summed floats often leave tiny leftovers like `0.1 + 0.2 - 0.3 \u2248 5.5e-17`, and small amounts like `-0.004` would otherwise show as `\"0.00\"` or `\"(0.00)\"`. If you only want an exact `0` to become `\"-\"`, it's a one-line change.\n\n**Tests:** I added `tests/test_report.py`. It checks the example values from your spec on a small table. It also checks, on the real `monthly_pnl` output from the sample ledger, that the input is unchanged, the index and columns are kept, and every cell is a string."
